WEBVTT

01:20.497 --> 01:22.499
(Alya Sometimes Hides Her Feelings in Russian)

01:30.966 --> 01:32.009
(Episode 3 And So, They Meet)

01:32.092 --> 01:33.051
(Episode 3 And So, They Meet)
I'm home.

01:33.076 --> 01:36.054
(Episode 3 And So, They Meet)
Welcome home, Alya.

01:40.184 --> 01:41.894
I'm home, Masha.

01:41.977 --> 01:42.811
Goodness.

01:42.895 --> 01:45.814
I told you to call me "big sis"
when we're in Japan.

01:46.148 --> 01:47.691
It's awkward to change it now.

01:48.775 --> 01:50.986
Alya, you're so cold.

01:54.489 --> 01:56.325
You seem to be in a bad mood.

01:56.658 --> 01:57.091
Did something happen?

01:58.869 --> 02:00.954
No, nothing happened.

02:01.371 --> 02:02.414
That's a lie.

02:02.664 --> 02:04.458
You can't fool your sister.

02:04.075 --> 02:07.002
Tell me. What's wrong?

02:07.461 --> 02:09.063
Nothing really happened.

02:10.088 --> 02:11.298
I just met Kuze

02:11.548 --> 02:14.051
and his childhood friend.

02:14.927 --> 02:16.047
Oh, that boy.

02:16.553 --> 02:17.387
What is it?

02:17.471 --> 02:18.514
Because...

02:19.681 --> 02:23.045
you always get a bit pouty
when you talk about him.

02:27.272 --> 02:28.774
I see.

02:29.399 --> 02:33.654
It seems that the boy who can move
Alya's heart has finally appeared.

02:34.279 --> 02:35.531
What are you saying?

02:35.989 --> 02:37.491
You like him, don't you?

02:37.574 --> 02:39.243
That Kuze guy.

02:39.785 --> 02:42.621
I don't know how you got that idea.

02:43.008 --> 02:45.123
But we're not like that.

02:45.916 --> 02:47.417
We are...

02:48.585 --> 02:49.545
That's right!

02:49.628 --> 02:50.712
We're friends.

02:52.381 --> 02:54.055
But why did you two become friends?

02:54.758 --> 02:57.886
You hate unserious people
who do things half-heartedly,

02:57.097 --> 02:58.887
don't you?

03:00.597 --> 03:02.015
Well, about that...

03:05.602 --> 03:07.396
(Six years ago)

03:07.813 --> 03:09.648
(Vladivostok)

03:10.482 --> 03:12.015
Please form groups and divide tasks

03:12.484 --> 03:14.945
to investigate nearby shops.

03:15.445 --> 03:17.114
The group that does the best

03:17.239 --> 03:18.574
will get the Excellence Award.

03:22.744 --> 03:26.748
So I'll take the clothing store and the bakery.

03:26.832 --> 03:31.128
Alya, you take the florist and the butcher shop.

03:31.712 --> 03:33.213
Okay, I got it.

03:33.063 --> 03:36.049
If we're going to do this,

03:36.133 --> 03:37.759
let's do our best!

03:41.013 --> 03:42.055
Excuse me.

03:42.043 --> 03:44.308
Yeah? Are you here on an errand?

03:44.391 --> 03:46.101
No, it's a school assignment.

03:46.056 --> 03:48.937
I'm doing research

03:49.062 --> 03:53.004
on different fields of work.

03:56.111 --> 03:57.362
This is it.

03:58.028 --> 03:59.074
Excuse me.

04:01.116 --> 04:02.618
The assignment?

04:02.993 --> 04:05.871
Sorry, I haven't done it yet.

04:06.371 --> 04:07.331
What?

04:07.789 --> 04:09.416
Why?

04:09.499 --> 04:12.092
It takes time to compile all the data.

04:13.003 --> 04:14.379
If you don't do it soon...

04:14.088 --> 04:16.798
There's still a week left.

04:16.882 --> 04:18.509
It's fine.

04:18.008 --> 04:20.719
No, it's not!

04:21.762 --> 04:25.039
I mean, a bakery sells bread.

04:25.474 --> 04:27.601
A clothing store sells clothes, right?

04:27.684 --> 04:29.144
That's right.

04:31.048 --> 04:33.899
It's so detailed!

04:35.234 --> 04:37.778
You're taking it too seriously.

04:38.007 --> 04:40.989
Alya, is it necessary to read all this?

04:44.243 --> 04:48.247
Why aren't you taking this seriously?

04:50.123 --> 04:51.208
If you don't like it,

04:51.291 --> 04:52.251
do it yourself!

04:52.334 --> 04:53.836
If you write casually like this,

04:53.919 --> 04:55.796
how are we going to get first place?

04:55.879 --> 04:57.381
Kids, stop it!

04:57.798 --> 05:00.008
Wait! Stop fighting!

05:09.081 --> 05:13.564
The Excellence Award
for the group presentation goes to...

05:14.231 --> 05:15.649
Group B.

05:15.732 --> 05:19.987
- Yay!
- That's great!

05:22.447 --> 05:25.492
If everyone takes things
seriously like I do...

05:26.159 --> 05:28.203
No, that's not right.

05:28.787 --> 05:31.029
I shouldn't have expected
anything from other people.

05:32.082 --> 05:33.292
Nobody in this world

05:33.375 --> 05:35.021
is willing to do things

05:35.294 --> 05:37.504
as serious and passionate as I am.

05:42.009 --> 05:43.001
If that's the case...

05:43.677 --> 05:44.803
If that's the case,

05:45.095 --> 05:47.222
I'll just do it all by myself.

06:02.007 --> 06:03.113
Hey.

06:03.197 --> 06:06.992
Did you really pass
that really difficult transfer exam?

06:07.409 --> 06:09.203
Well, yes.

06:09.286 --> 06:11.496
Kujou, your Japanese is really good.

06:11.058 --> 06:13.415
Have you lived in Japan before?

06:13.498 --> 06:15.501
I did five years ago.

06:17.294 --> 06:19.213
Kujou, let's talk later.

06:23.967 --> 06:26.022
How can he sleep after all that noise?

06:27.554 --> 06:29.681
Excuse me. Class is starting now.

06:33.769 --> 06:36.073
Are you the transfer student
who spoke at the entrance ceremony?

06:37.064 --> 06:38.044
Yes.

06:39.066 --> 06:41.401
I'm Alisa Mikhailovna Kujou.

06:41.086 --> 06:42.903
Nice to meet you.

06:44.071 --> 06:45.822
I'm Masachika Kuze.

06:46.198 --> 06:47.824
Nice to meet you.

06:50.827 --> 06:53.205
Hey, Hikaru. You're in this class too.

06:53.288 --> 06:54.373
I've always been here.

06:54.581 --> 06:56.005
By the way, Takeshi's in this class too.

06:56.583 --> 06:58.168
You're right.

07:00.254 --> 07:01.171
(Science)

07:02.089 --> 07:04.132
I forgot my textbook.

07:04.466 --> 07:06.301
Sorry, Hikaru. Can I borrow yours?

07:06.385 --> 07:07.344
Sure.

07:07.678 --> 07:08.679
(Physical Education)

07:12.891 --> 07:14.056
I'm so tired from running.

07:14.643 --> 07:15.561
Me too.

07:16.077 --> 07:17.729
(Physical Education)

07:17.813 --> 07:18.814
(Math)

07:21.358 --> 07:23.068
This is a prestigious school,

07:23.151 --> 07:25.612
so does every school
have a student like this?

07:34.454 --> 07:35.706
(14 Days Until the School Festival
Haunted House Confirmed)

07:35.789 --> 07:36.707
Let's see.

07:37.082 --> 07:39.501
We need some door panels
to partition a path.

07:39.585 --> 07:41.712
What should we do
about the ghost costumes?

07:41.795 --> 07:43.797
Wait! Let me think about it one by one.

07:44.089 --> 07:47.342
Goodness, I didn't expect it
to be so troublesome.

07:47.426 --> 07:48.051
Indeed.

07:50.095 --> 07:51.889
Kujou, you're not going home yet?

07:52.139 --> 07:54.683
No, I still want to work on it.

07:54.975 --> 07:55.976
I see.

07:56.059 --> 07:57.144
See you tomorrow.

07:58.187 --> 07:59.646
Can we make it in time?

08:00.355 --> 08:02.274
But it's just a school festival.

08:02.608 --> 08:04.985
There's no point in taking it seriously.

08:06.778 --> 08:08.614
It's the same as back then.

08:11.241 --> 08:12.242
Ouch!

08:15.245 --> 08:18.332
I just want to give it my all.

08:18.916 --> 08:21.418
I just don't want to give up.

08:22.461 --> 08:24.296
In order to achieve that,

08:25.881 --> 08:26.924
even if I'm alone,

08:27.341 --> 08:28.467
it's not a big deal.

08:33.847 --> 08:35.933
Sure enough, you're still here.

08:36.035 --> 08:38.393
Kuze, why are you still at school?

08:38.852 --> 08:41.104
Good work. Well, something came up.

08:42.356 --> 08:44.399
Kujou, you should also go home.

08:44.942 --> 08:46.151
We can do

08:46.235 --> 08:48.403
these tasks together tomorrow.

08:48.862 --> 08:50.028
Don't worry about it.

08:50.531 --> 08:52.157
I'll finish it up and go home.

08:52.241 --> 08:53.283
Don't mind me.

08:54.034 --> 08:56.286
Well... Okay.

08:56.828 --> 08:58.058
Regarding costume-making,

08:58.664 --> 09:01.375
I've asked for help
from the handicrafts club.

09:01.583 --> 09:02.417
What?

09:02.501 --> 09:05.045
Also, here.
A usage permit for the boarding house.

09:05.462 --> 09:07.013
If we can hold an overnight event,

09:07.214 --> 09:09.055
I'm sure the slackers
will get motivated too.

09:09.967 --> 09:12.302
The boarding house? How did you get it?

09:12.886 --> 09:14.763
I asked the former president for help

09:14.847 --> 09:16.431
and used her connections.

09:16.849 --> 09:18.642
The handicrafts club said they'd help out

09:18.725 --> 09:19.852
if I lent them some boys.

09:20.185 --> 09:21.027
If I tell the boys

09:21.353 --> 09:24.231
that it's a good chance to show
how reliable they are to the girls,

09:24.314 --> 09:26.316
I'm sure they will gladly do it.

09:28.277 --> 09:29.361
Anyway,

09:29.444 --> 09:31.071
let's go home for today.

09:31.405 --> 09:33.323
There's no point in working so hard

09:33.407 --> 09:34.533
on your own, right?

09:38.078 --> 09:39.705
What do you mean by that?

09:41.373 --> 09:42.499
If I...

09:42.791 --> 09:44.501
If I'm going to participate,

09:44.668 --> 09:47.171
I want to show everyone
an excellent product!

09:47.254 --> 09:48.038
I don't want to present

09:48.463 --> 09:51.008
a half-baked product on the day itself.

09:51.633 --> 09:54.072
I don't want to compromise at all!

09:55.012 --> 09:58.515
(Haunted House)
But I also know that it's just

09:58.599 --> 09:59.683
my wishful thinking.

10:00.392 --> 10:01.226
I know that

10:01.031 --> 10:04.605
everyone doesn't care
about this as much as I do.

10:04.771 --> 10:07.691
That's why I'll work diligently
on behalf of them too!

10:07.774 --> 10:10.694
What's wrong with that?

10:13.078 --> 10:16.002
You're working
in the wrong direction, right?

10:16.408 --> 10:17.367
What?

10:17.451 --> 10:20.579
The school festival
isn't something you do alone.

10:21.163 --> 10:23.916
It's something you complete together.

10:24.458 --> 10:26.376
If you want to make an excellent product,

10:26.046 --> 10:30.088
you should think more about
how to motivate everyone.

10:30.255 --> 10:31.381
That's...

10:35.594 --> 10:37.179
That being said,

10:37.262 --> 10:39.089
anyone would get mad if they heard that.

10:43.685 --> 10:44.686
I'm sorry.

10:45.145 --> 10:47.231
I know you're doing your best.

10:57.407 --> 10:58.367
I'm going home.

10:58.867 --> 11:00.911
Okay, thank you for your hard work.

11:04.081 --> 11:05.082
What was that?

11:05.582 --> 11:06.834
What was that?

11:16.076 --> 11:18.011
What's his deal?

11:19.179 --> 11:20.931
(Boarding House!)

11:21.014 --> 11:21.932
So that's why!

11:22.391 --> 11:24.226
While we prepare for the school festival,

11:24.476 --> 11:27.688
let's test our courage with hide-and-seek
on the school premises at night!

11:27.771 --> 11:29.147
This will be

11:29.231 --> 11:32.109
our pre-pre-pre-party
for the school festival!

11:36.196 --> 11:37.614
(Do Your Best!
Six Days Until the School Festival)

11:55.674 --> 11:57.092
(Seiren School Festival)

12:07.186 --> 12:09.605
(Excellence Award)

12:24.453 --> 12:26.622
Good work, Kujou.

12:27.372 --> 12:30.501
This school is really old-fashioned
when it comes to this.

12:30.918 --> 12:32.336
Can't believe they still do

12:32.419 --> 12:33.712
after-party folk dance.

12:35.038 --> 12:37.009
Can I sit next to you?

12:37.966 --> 12:39.218
Sure thing.

12:39.468 --> 12:40.719
But aren't you dancing?

12:41.178 --> 12:43.305
You'll be a hot pick, won't you?

12:44.056 --> 12:46.517
Do you not know how to folk dance?

12:46.006 --> 12:47.726
How rude.

12:47.809 --> 12:50.479
I may not look like it,
but I did ballet when I was a kid.

12:50.771 --> 12:52.314
I can learn

12:52.397 --> 12:53.815
that simple dance in no time.

12:54.316 --> 12:55.734
But it's troublesome,

12:55.817 --> 12:57.402
so I said I don't know as an excuse

12:57.486 --> 12:59.488
and turned down everyone's invitations.

12:59.988 --> 13:02.199
That must have been hard for you.

13:02.574 --> 13:03.408
Not really.

13:03.492 --> 13:04.576
I'm used to it.

13:04.066 --> 13:05.953
So it's not a hassle at all.

13:06.036 --> 13:07.496
I see.

13:07.579 --> 13:09.498
You're indeed the solitary princess.

13:09.581 --> 13:10.582
What's that?

13:10.874 --> 13:12.125
What? Don't you know?

13:12.459 --> 13:13.877
That's what the other students

13:13.961 --> 13:15.712
have been calling you lately.

13:17.673 --> 13:19.591
You don't seem too happy about it.

13:19.967 --> 13:22.761
Yes, maybe I'm not.

13:22.845 --> 13:25.514
Why? Is it because
they mock your lack of friends?

13:25.597 --> 13:27.307
That's not it.

13:27.391 --> 13:29.726
Can you not say it
in such a derogatory way?

13:30.143 --> 13:31.186
Sorry.

13:31.687 --> 13:35.232
What I don't like is the word "princess".

13:35.607 --> 13:37.109
Isn't that a compliment?

13:37.568 --> 13:39.695
It makes me sound like
I'm a fairytale princess

13:39.778 --> 13:41.697
who knows no hardships.

13:42.281 --> 13:45.409
Well, is that how you interpret it?

13:45.909 --> 13:48.996
In terms of appearance and talent,

13:49.079 --> 13:51.164
I'm indeed more gifted than others.

13:52.004 --> 13:52.875
But

13:52.958 --> 13:55.711
I've never thought
of resting on my laurels.

13:56.086 --> 13:57.838
That's like saying all my efforts so far

13:57.921 --> 14:00.034
are credited solely to being born better.

14:00.424 --> 14:01.003
I don't like it.

14:01.842 --> 14:03.218
I get it now.

14:03.076 --> 14:07.222
I won't call you that from now on.

14:07.556 --> 14:08.064
I see.

14:10.726 --> 14:12.811
Thank you, Kuze.

14:13.312 --> 14:14.313
For what?

14:14.688 --> 14:17.691
- I was wrong this time.
- Can you really dance?

14:18.066 --> 14:20.194
If I insisted on doing it alone,

14:20.444 --> 14:24.615
I wouldn't have been able to enjoy
the school festival as much as I did.

14:25.866 --> 14:27.951
And I'm sorry.

14:28.016 --> 14:30.287
Back then, I took it out on you.

14:30.495 --> 14:32.039
Don't worry about it.

14:32.122 --> 14:34.291
All I did was help with the paperwork.

14:34.374 --> 14:36.001
I'm not like Takeshi and Kujou,

14:36.084 --> 14:38.212
who always work harder than the rest.

14:38.337 --> 14:40.172
It's been bothering me.

14:40.464 --> 14:42.382
As an apology for my outburst

14:42.466 --> 14:44.301
and as a token of gratitude,

14:44.551 --> 14:46.072
I'd like to do something for you.

14:47.179 --> 14:48.805
Is there anything you want?

14:49.306 --> 14:50.807
A token of gratitude?

14:50.974 --> 14:53.101
Don't say you don't need it.

14:56.522 --> 14:57.356
Right.

14:57.689 --> 14:58.069
In Russia,

14:58.774 --> 15:01.818
you have a habit of calling each other
by special nicknames, right?

15:01.902 --> 15:03.403
Why did you mention that suddenly?

15:03.654 --> 15:04.821
Is it Alisha?

15:05.072 --> 15:06.782
No, is it Alishka?

15:06.865 --> 15:07.824
It's Alya.

15:07.908 --> 15:10.035
My family calls me Alya.

15:10.369 --> 15:11.286
I see.

15:11.037 --> 15:13.288
Well then, what I want

15:13.372 --> 15:15.541
is for you to let me call you Alya too.

15:15.624 --> 15:16.005
What's that?

15:16.583 --> 15:18.168
How's that a token of gratitude?

15:18.046 --> 15:20.879
You're the class idol
that everyone looks up to.

15:20.963 --> 15:23.173
As the only guy
who can call you by your nickname,

15:23.257 --> 15:24.299
I'll be very happy.

15:24.675 --> 15:25.801
Are you stupid?

15:25.884 --> 15:27.427
Thank you very much.

15:27.511 --> 15:28.345
Gross.

15:28.679 --> 15:30.597
Excuse me, Kujou.

15:31.807 --> 15:34.017
If you don't mind, will you dance with me?

15:34.101 --> 15:36.562
Hey, don't get ahead of me!

15:36.645 --> 15:39.398
Alisa, I've been interested
in you for a long time!

15:39.481 --> 15:40.983
Will you dance with me?

15:41.066 --> 15:43.652
You're confessing your love now?
That's unfair!

15:44.069 --> 15:45.112
I'm sorry.

15:45.195 --> 15:47.531
- I can't dance.
- It's okay.

15:47.614 --> 15:50.284
Just let your body move to the music.

15:50.367 --> 15:52.035
That's right. Don't worry.

15:52.119 --> 15:53.012
I can't dance either.

15:53.203 --> 15:55.163
Go with the vibe
and you'll dance just fine.

15:55.247 --> 15:56.079
Do you guys...

15:59.084 --> 16:00.794
Sorry, but she has plans with me.

16:03.797 --> 16:05.299
Let's go, Alya.

16:05.799 --> 16:07.092
Hold on...

16:14.975 --> 16:17.811
My heartbeat is so loud.

16:19.563 --> 16:21.857
By the way, didn't you just say

16:21.094 --> 16:23.066
that you learned ballet

16:23.015 --> 16:25.694
and you could dance folk just by watching?

16:25.944 --> 16:27.321
Yes.

16:27.571 --> 16:28.053
Well then,

16:28.614 --> 16:30.282
may I see how you dance,

16:30.574 --> 16:31.909
Your Highness?

16:34.119 --> 16:35.204
Bring it on.

16:46.059 --> 16:48.383
Good morning, Alya.

16:50.969 --> 16:52.679
What's wrong?

16:52.763 --> 16:55.265
You're looking at me like I'm trash.

16:55.349 --> 16:56.308
Scumbag.

16:56.391 --> 16:57.976
That's going too far!

17:00.604 --> 17:03.069
He was so cool yesterday.

17:03.815 --> 17:04.983
(Excellence Award)

17:06.401 --> 17:07.736
I see.

17:08.195 --> 17:10.739
So you fell in love with him?

17:10.822 --> 17:11.074
That's so romantic.

17:11.099 --> 17:13.784
I told you it's not.

17:13.867 --> 17:15.327
Were you listening to me?

17:16.495 --> 17:19.998
But it sounds like
you two are falling for each other.

17:20.029 --> 17:22.084
Don't describe it in such a strange way.

17:22.167 --> 17:24.503
Didn't I just say we're friends?

17:25.963 --> 17:29.299
Going from friends
to lovers is the way to go.

17:30.005 --> 17:32.511
It's the same for me and Saa.

17:32.097 --> 17:34.012
Right?

17:36.765 --> 17:38.006
But you're right.

17:38.976 --> 17:41.311
I admit that he's capable.

17:41.395 --> 17:43.105
And he's trustworthy.

17:43.048 --> 17:46.817
A guy who gives his all
when he needs to is really cool.

17:47.442 --> 17:48.819
Saa is like that too.

17:49.194 --> 17:51.154
When I was attacked by a dog before,

17:51.238 --> 17:52.823
the way he came to save me was--

17:52.906 --> 17:55.033
If you want to be lovey-dovey,
please get out.

17:55.242 --> 17:58.012
Goodness, you're so cold!

18:02.374 --> 18:03.917
(Student Council Office)
Excuse me.

18:04.501 --> 18:05.794
Kuze.

18:05.878 --> 18:06.712
Sorry.

18:06.795 --> 18:08.922
Thanks for coming all the way here.

18:09.006 --> 18:12.384
No problem. I'm just filling in for Yuki.

18:13.093 --> 18:15.554
Oh, are you Kuze?

18:16.018 --> 18:18.765
I'm Maria Mikhailovna Kujou.

18:18.849 --> 18:21.852
I'm Alya's older sister
and the student council secretary.

18:22.144 --> 18:23.052
Nice to meet you.

18:24.062 --> 18:24.098
Nice to meet you.

18:25.147 --> 18:27.399
Alya has been a great help to me.

18:27.858 --> 18:31.032
Kujou, I heard I'm supposed
to go shopping with you today.

18:31.057 --> 18:34.198
Just Masha will do.

18:34.489 --> 18:36.408
If you're Alya's friend,

18:36.491 --> 18:38.785
you're my friend too.

18:38.911 --> 18:40.245
I see.

18:40.329 --> 18:42.414
Then I'll call you Masha.

18:47.377 --> 18:49.588
Nice to meet you.

18:51.381 --> 18:52.925
What's wrong?

18:54.384 --> 18:56.047
Kuze, what's your name?

18:56.553 --> 18:57.471
What?

18:57.679 --> 18:58.764
I'm Masachika.

18:58.847 --> 19:01.975
M-a-s-a-c-h-i-k-a.

19:03.477 --> 19:05.103
Masachika?

19:06.688 --> 19:07.689
What's wrong?

19:07.773 --> 19:10.108
Is there something on Kuze's back?

19:10.192 --> 19:11.193
President.

19:11.276 --> 19:12.011
I guess you wanna ask

19:12.194 --> 19:14.196
"Is there something on his face?"

19:14.279 --> 19:15.531
You're amazing.

19:19.409 --> 19:20.494
I'm sorry.

19:20.869 --> 19:24.498
I was just thinking,
"So this is Alya's friend."

19:24.581 --> 19:25.415
and got distracted.

19:27.793 --> 19:29.092
Well then, let's go.

19:31.088 --> 19:34.007
Excuse me. What did you just say?

19:36.677 --> 19:37.678
I'm sorry.

19:37.097 --> 19:39.972
I just said, "Let's go."

19:40.389 --> 19:41.598
All right.

19:42.057 --> 19:44.518
All right, President. We'll be going now.

19:44.601 --> 19:46.019
I'm counting on you.

19:49.106 --> 19:50.816
Should we buy a diffuser?

19:50.899 --> 19:53.777
No, we shouldn't put that
in the student council office.

19:53.986 --> 19:55.821
It's better to keep it in your own room.

19:55.904 --> 19:57.114
My goodness!

19:58.782 --> 20:00.659
This stuffed kitty

20:00.742 --> 20:02.703
looks just like Alya!

20:04.329 --> 20:05.163
Right.

20:05.247 --> 20:09.293
Why don't we choose a few dolls based on
the image of the student council members

20:09.376 --> 20:10.335
and display them?

20:10.419 --> 20:12.171
Is our office some kind of dreamland?

20:12.754 --> 20:14.059
Aside from the other female members,

20:14.673 --> 20:17.759
I'm sure the president can't stand it.

20:17.843 --> 20:19.178
The president?

20:19.553 --> 20:22.306
It's this lion gentleman with glasses.

20:22.389 --> 20:23.432
No, I mean...

20:23.515 --> 20:24.892
The resemblance is uncanny!

20:25.893 --> 20:27.394
Let's go with this one.

20:27.477 --> 20:28.077
No, even if it's similar,

20:28.854 --> 20:31.023
we don't normally display
stuffed animals, right?

20:31.523 --> 20:32.691
What?

20:32.774 --> 20:35.194
No, I'm the one who's confused.

20:36.695 --> 20:37.905
I understand.

20:38.572 --> 20:40.824
But this kitty is cute.

20:40.908 --> 20:42.201
I want to buy it for myself.

20:42.868 --> 20:44.661
If you combine the receipts,

20:44.745 --> 20:46.914
the bookkeeper Alya will scold you.

20:51.668 --> 20:54.671
This won't do. She does as she pleases.

20:54.088 --> 20:56.715
Has she always been like this?

20:57.174 --> 20:59.009
Then Alya

20:59.259 --> 21:01.512
must be having a hard time too.

21:04.181 --> 21:05.891
Kuze, this is the shop.

21:05.974 --> 21:06.892
Okay.

21:07.351 --> 21:09.311
Masha, let me carry that for you.

21:10.229 --> 21:11.313
Thank you.

21:11.772 --> 21:14.483
In that case,
please take good care of Alya Kitty.

21:15.317 --> 21:17.903
Alya Kitty?

21:19.613 --> 21:21.615
Goodness, it looks good on you.

21:21.698 --> 21:23.492
Your taste is a little bit weird, right?

21:23.867 --> 21:25.285
Here, say cheese.

21:25.041 --> 21:26.828
No, I won't let you take it.

21:26.912 --> 21:29.289
Why not?

21:29.373 --> 21:31.625
Come on. Aren't you going to buy tea?

21:31.708 --> 21:33.794
All right.

21:36.797 --> 21:37.631
Here you go.

21:37.714 --> 21:39.091
Thank you.

21:39.174 --> 21:41.718
This is the first flush tea,
so it's a bit astringent.

21:41.802 --> 21:42.097
Hey, Kuze.

21:43.679 --> 21:45.138
Which one do you think is better?

21:45.556 --> 21:48.475
I don't know much about black tea.

21:48.767 --> 21:49.726
Is that so?

21:51.061 --> 21:54.398
If it was Yuki who grew up
under our mother's guidance,

21:54.481 --> 21:56.984
I'm sure she could give
some advice at a time like this.

21:57.901 --> 21:58.777
But I...

21:59.736 --> 22:01.071
I'm sorry, Masachika.

22:01.655 --> 22:02.865
Your mother and I

22:02.948 --> 22:04.366
have decided to live separately

22:04.449 --> 22:05.784
from now on.

22:07.661 --> 22:08.912
I see.

22:09.058 --> 22:10.414
In that case,

22:10.497 --> 22:11.415
I...

22:11.498 --> 22:14.209
I'll go with you, Dad.

22:18.088 --> 22:19.798
I'm sorry, Masachika.

22:20.757 --> 22:23.051
I've decided to stay in this house.

22:25.047 --> 22:26.513
Kuze?

22:28.039 --> 22:29.006
What's the matter?

22:30.001 --> 22:32.102
No, it's nothing.

22:34.229 --> 22:36.023
You look like you're in pain.

22:39.443 --> 22:40.402
What?

22:42.362 --> 22:43.488
It's okay.

22:44.072 --> 22:45.049
There, there.

22:47.159 --> 22:48.066
What is this feeling?

22:49.286 --> 22:50.829
It feels familiar.

22:51.455 --> 22:53.081
It kind of puts me at ease.

22:55.918 --> 22:57.294
Wait, it's hot!

22:57.377 --> 22:58.212
It's hot!

22:58.587 --> 22:59.421
What?

22:59.505 --> 23:00.714
Masha!

23:00.797 --> 23:02.216
Your tea touched my back!

23:02.299 --> 23:03.175
Sorry!

23:03.258 --> 23:06.022
It's freaking hot!

23:06.303 --> 23:08.222
Oh, my!
